{
  "dom_id": "question-184275",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "Prove that $11n+3$ is odd provided that $n$ is an even integer.\n\nLet $n$ be an even integer. Then, $n=\\,${{field-1}} for some integer $a.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11n+3 & ={{field-2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-3}}.  Since $a$ is {{field-4}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-5}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11n+3 & ={{field-6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is one larger than a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $11n+3$ is {{field-7}}.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
